<div class="masthead"><span class="name">{{ section.settings.masthead | default: 'The Everyday Ritual' }}</span></div>
<div class="crumb">Home &rsaquo; Skin &rsaquo; Simple Routines</div>

<div class="wrap">

  <h1>{{ section.settings.headline | default: "It's Not \"Just My Face.\" It Was Her Skin." }}</h1>
  <div class="dek">{{ section.settings.dek | default: "A birthday photo she almost scrolled past turned into the thing that changed how a friend saw her, twice, without knowing it." }}</div>

  <div class="summary">A blurry group-chat photo made one woman stop scrolling. Nine sleep-filled hours, and she still looked exhausted in it. What she found out about why has more to do with chemistry than sleep.</div>

  <div class="byline">Written by <b>{{ section.settings.byline | default: 'Julie B.' }}</b> &middot; {{ section.settings.byline_date | default: 'July 2026' }}</div>

  {%- if section.settings.hero_image != blank -%}
    <div class="hero-img">{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', alt: 'A phone screen showing a paused video call photo' }}
    <div class="caption">The photo that started it: mid-laugh, nine hours of sleep, and still looked exhausted.</div></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p>My cousin Renata posted the photos from her birthday dinner the next morning, and I scrolled straight past mine twice before I went back and looked.</p>
  <p>Mid-laugh. Candlelight. A glass halfway to my mouth. I looked exhausted. I'd slept nine hours that night, I remember because I'd bragged about it at the table.</p>
  <p>If you've ever looked at a photo of yourself on a day you felt completely fine and not recognized what you saw, you know that specific, confusing kind of unsettled. That's actually what sent me looking for an answer, and <a class="cta-link" href="{{ section.settings.pdp_url | default: 'https://trybasline.com/products/whipped-tallow-honey-balm' }}">I found it in a jar a friend had already been using for months</a>.</p>
  <p>I went back through my camera roll, not obsessively, just curious now. A photo from my kid's game two weeks earlier, same flatness around the eyes. One from a work lunch in June, same thing. It wasn't one bad photo. It was a pattern I'd never noticed because I was never the one holding the camera.</p>

  <h2>The comment that stuck</h2>
  <p>About a month before that birthday dinner, my neighbor Priya looked at me over her coffee and said, "You doing okay? You look wiped." She wasn't being unkind, she said it quick, the way you'd mention spinach in someone's teeth, already moving to the next thing. I said I was fine. I was fine. I let it go. It sat there anyway.</p>

  {%- if section.settings.diagram_image != blank -%}
    <div class="mid-img">{{ section.settings.diagram_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'Water evaporates, fat absorbs diagram' }}
    <div class="caption">The whole difference, in one picture: water sits on top and evaporates. Fat absorbs in and stays.</div></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <h2>What my sister-in-law told me</h2>
  <p>I mentioned the photos to Dana at a family thing, half a joke. "I look tired in every picture lately and I'm sleeping fine." She didn't laugh it off. She asked if I'd actually looked at my moisturizer, or just at my face.</p>
  <p>Skin makes its own oil. It always has. Most people never connect what's changing on their face to what's changed underneath. Here's the part that isn't a theory, it's just chemistry: nearly every moisturizer lists water first on the label, meaning water is the single biggest thing in the bottle. Water evaporates. Put it on at 7am and by mid-morning a lot of it is already gone. That's not a bad batch or the wrong brand, that's what water does, in any bottle, from any company. <a class="cta-link" href="{{ section.settings.pdp_url | default: 'https://trybasline.com/products/whipped-tallow-honey-balm' }}">Here's what Dana switched to instead.</a></p>
  <p>Fat doesn't have that problem the same way. Tallow specifically is close in structure to the oil skin already makes on its own, so instead of sitting on top waiting to evaporate, it gets absorbed the way skin absorbs its own oil. Four ingredients. Dana had been on it eight months by the time she told me.</p>

  {%- if section.settings.jar_image != blank -%}
    <div class="mid-img">{{ section.settings.jar_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: 'Whipped tallow and honey balm jar' }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <h3>"Tallow. Like cow fat. On my face."</h3>
  <p>That was my first reaction. Dana's answer: "I know how it sounds. I made the same face you're making right now. Just try it." I ordered one that night. $49.99. Free shipping. 60-day money-back guarantee, use the whole jar, nothing to send back if it doesn't work out.</p>

  <h2>The second conversation</h2>
  <p>Day 1, it melted into my palm like warm honey. Day 4, I woke up and touched my face before I even opened my eyes, soft in a way that felt underneath, not on top. Day 9, I scrolled back through the same camera roll and didn't flinch at a new photo. Day 21, I realized I hadn't opened my front camera to "check" myself before a video call in almost two weeks.</p>
  <p>Priya and I got coffee again about two months after her first comment, same table, same cups. She stopped mid-sip and said, "Okay, wait, what did you do? You look really good. Like rested." I hadn't slept any differently. That was sort of her point.</p>

  {%- if section.settings.review_quote != blank -%}
  <blockquote>"{{ section.settings.review_quote }}"<span class="who">{{ section.settings.review_author | default: 'Verified buyer' }}</span></blockquote>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p><a class="cta-link" href="{{ section.settings.pdp_url | default: 'https://trybasline.com/products/whipped-tallow-honey-balm' }}">You can check price and availability here.</a></p>

  <h2>Final thoughts</h2>
  <p>There's a 60-day money-back guarantee, use the whole jar, and if it doesn't do anything, email them and get every dollar back, nothing to send back first. That's the part that got me over the "beef fat, seriously?" hump.</p>
  <p>I'm not telling you a jar of cow fat will fix your life. I'm telling you about a birthday photo I almost scrolled past, and a coffee with Priya two months later where she said the exact opposite of what she'd said the first time, without me bringing any of it up.</p>

  <a class="cta-btn" href="{{ section.settings.pdp_url | default: 'https://trybasline.com/products/whipped-tallow-honey-balm' }}">Check Availability &amp; See The Jar &raquo;</a>
  <div class="cta-sub">Free shipping &middot; 60-day money-back guarantee &middot; 4 ingredients</div>

  <p class="ps"><b>P.S.</b> My tally of "you look tired" comments hasn't moved in months, and I don't think about it enough anymore to notice that on purpose.</p>

</div>

